    "heightMetres": 14,
    "transparency": 0,
    "_transparency": "Opaque, not 0.25. The wall was semi-transparent so the border treeline could be glimpsed through it, which cost 5729 square metres of overdraw -- semi-transparent surfaces cannot early-out of the depth test -- and showed almost nothing at 75% opacity. The treeline is 24 m tall and this wall is 14 m, so ten metres of spire still stands above it against the sky, which is the part of a treeline you actually read. Opaque wall, visible trees, no overdraw."
  },
